{
  "case_id": "2008-07-513",
  "document_hash": "2acc9027c86b657928a681526cfe4d70d75e57b67ce3878dc83945d91d621dc4",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2008-07-513",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2acc9027c86b657928a681526cfe4d70d75e57b67ce3878dc83945d91d621dc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2acc9027c86b-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In February 2004, the Dale County circuit clerk told the local sheriff's department that the court was recalling a warrant that had been issued earlier for Petitioner's arrest. Having received that notice, someone in the sheriff's department physically removed the warrant from the file and physically took the warrant back to the court clerk's office. But no one either then or later in the sheriff's department ever updated the computer file to indicate that the record had -- that the warrant had been recalled. As a result of that police department error, the Petitioner in this case was subject to a warrantless arrest for which there was no probable cause five months later."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-07-513",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2acc9027c86b657928a681526cfe4d70d75e57b67ce3878dc83945d91d621dc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2acc9027c86b-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Does your argument depend on the quality of the recordkeeping in this particular department? I thought your argument would apply even if this department had excellent recordkeeping procedures but nevertheless made a mistake in this instance."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2008-07-513",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2acc9027c86b657928a681526cfe4d70d75e57b67ce3878dc83945d91d621dc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2acc9027c86b-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We're asking to you apply Arizona v. Evans."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-513",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2acc9027c86b657928a681526cfe4d70d75e57b67ce3878dc83945d91d621dc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2acc9027c86b-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I thought negligence is irrelevant here. I think if the police department was wrong, even if they had been very careful but for some reason or other they made a mistake -- so you're arguing for shear causality, not for negligence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-07-513",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2acc9027c86b657928a681526cfe4d70d75e57b67ce3878dc83945d91d621dc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2acc9027c86b-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, what's the justification for drawing a distinction between a court employee and everybody who works for the police department? Suppose the person who makes the mistake in the police department is a -- a person who holds a unionized position where advancement is based purely on seniority, or it's a civil service position where the person is -- is totally protected from any sort of adverse job consequences as a result of displeasure about or pleasure about how the job is being -- being performed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-513",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2acc9027c86b657928a681526cfe4d70d75e57b67ce3878dc83945d91d621dc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2acc9027c86b-0001-0002",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the police will not keep good records unless -- unless we let the criminals go."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-513",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2acc9027c86b657928a681526cfe4d70d75e57b67ce3878dc83945d91d621dc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2acc9027c86b-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We don't know if these records are good, bad, or indifferent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-513",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2acc9027c86b657928a681526cfe4d70d75e57b67ce3878dc83945d91d621dc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2acc9027c86b-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "May I interrupt you there? I mean, why do you say that? I mean, we -- we have -- just getting outside the criminal law for a minute, we -- we've got a whole system of personal liability law in which the theory is that, in effect, requiring compensation for negligence, even though it is not an act of bad faith or malice, is -- is going to affect conduct."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-513",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2acc9027c86b657928a681526cfe4d70d75e57b67ce3878dc83945d91d621dc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2acc9027c86b-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is there a 1983 violation here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dreeben",
      "case_id": "2008-07-513",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2acc9027c86b657928a681526cfe4d70d75e57b67ce3878dc83945d91d621dc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2acc9027c86b-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "An isolated and negligent police clerical error in the maintenance of warrant records should not lead to suppression."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dreeben",
      "case_id": "2008-07-513",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2acc9027c86b657928a681526cfe4d70d75e57b67ce3878dc83945d91d621dc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2acc9027c86b-0002-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DREEBEN: I would reserve the right to argue that the exclusionary rule's costs outweigh its benefits even if that is shown in a particular case because there are a myriad of other reasons why the police would have an incentive to improve that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-513",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2acc9027c86b657928a681526cfe4d70d75e57b67ce3878dc83945d91d621dc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2acc9027c86b-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: In Hudson versus Michigan, didn't the Court engage in a very broad balancing of the social costs and the potential for increase in violations in saying that there was no necessity for the suppression rule in the no-knock case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-07-513",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2acc9027c86b657928a681526cfe4d70d75e57b67ce3878dc83945d91d621dc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2acc9027c86b-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Can I use 30 seconds of your eight minutes because I want some clarity on this."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-07-513",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2acc9027c86b657928a681526cfe4d70d75e57b67ce3878dc83945d91d621dc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2acc9027c86b-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Divide in your mind two separate things: The nature of the bad conduct: is it negligent, reckless, deliberate; and the other question is who engaged in it -- a police department official or some other official?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Karlan",
      "case_id": "2008-07-513",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2acc9027c86b657928a681526cfe4d70d75e57b67ce3878dc83945d91d621dc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2acc9027c86b-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. KARLAN: The answer to your question, Justice Breyer, is if the police officer in your hypothetical was negligent the evidence would be suppressed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-513",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2acc9027c86b657928a681526cfe4d70d75e57b67ce3878dc83945d91d621dc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2acc9027c86b-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: And the definition of negligence is that he was not objectively reasonable?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Karlan",
      "case_id": "2008-07-513",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2acc9027c86b657928a681526cfe4d70d75e57b67ce3878dc83945d91d621dc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2acc9027c86b-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. KARLAN: And the rule we are asking for here -- the narrow rule for our Petitioner is when you have negligent error by police officials, you suppress but as Justice Scalia pointed out in my colloquy with him earlier, that rule is perhaps slightly less workable than a rule that says all error."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Karlan",
      "case_id": "2008-07-513",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "document_hash": "2acc9027c86b657928a681526cfe4d70d75e57b67ce3878dc83945d91d621dc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2acc9027c86b-0003-0005",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "one out of six warrants is invalid, one out of seven warrants is invalid, but that's okay."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-07-513",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "2acc9027c86b657928a681526cfe4d70d75e57b67ce3878dc83945d91d621dc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2acc9027c86b-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Isn't your rule also going to require hearings. If negligence is required --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-513",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "2acc9027c86b657928a681526cfe4d70d75e57b67ce3878dc83945d91d621dc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2acc9027c86b-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Suppose it were an agency like INS or Customs in which they have many people that are not sworn officers or some that are, does it make a difference who answered the phone?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Karlan",
      "case_id": "2008-07-513",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2acc9027c86b657928a681526cfe4d70d75e57b67ce3878dc83945d91d621dc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2acc9027c86b-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We are arguing for negligent --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Karlan",
      "case_id": "2008-07-513",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "2acc9027c86b657928a681526cfe4d70d75e57b67ce3878dc83945d91d621dc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2acc9027c86b-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our rule is, I think, a clean, narrow rule."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court Clerk",
      "case_id": "2008-07-513",
      "confidence": 0.98,
      "document_hash": "2acc9027c86b657928a681526cfe4d70d75e57b67ce3878dc83945d91d621dc4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2acc9027c86b-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2008-07-513",
      "confidence": 0.0,
